WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.101 --> 00:00:08.123
In this video you’ll get your team onto the map.

2
00:00:08.123 --> 00:00:10.805
Employees join with a site code.

3
00:00:10.805 --> 00:00:13.235
Managers get access by email.

4
00:00:13.688 --> 00:00:17.268
Open Sites & people.

5
00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:22.612
Every site has a six-character code, like this one for Sample Garage.

6
00:00:22.612 --> 00:00:24.455
Give it to your employees.

7
00:00:24.455 --> 00:00:29.702
They sign in, type the code, and they can view that site’s published maps.

8
00:00:29.702 --> 00:00:31.616
They can’t change anything.

9
00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:37.943
If a code gets passed around too widely, choose New code.

10
00:00:37.943 --> 00:00:45.670
The old one stops working, and people who already joined keep their access.

11
00:00:46.125 --> 00:00:50.748
For managers, use Give someone access.

12
00:00:50.748 --> 00:00:53.425
Type their work email.

13
00:00:53.876 --> 00:01:00.957
Pick their access. A site manager can edit and publish maps at their own site.

14
00:01:00.957 --> 00:01:04.316
A regional manager covers every site.

15
00:01:04.316 --> 00:01:06.676
An employee can only view.

16
00:01:07.127 --> 00:01:11.527
Pick the site, and choose Give access.

17
00:01:11.981 --> 00:01:15.204
The app doesn’t email them for you.

18
00:01:15.204 --> 00:01:19.625
Choose Copy invite message and send it yourself.

19
00:01:19.625 --> 00:01:23.861
It has the link and tells them how to sign in.

20
00:01:24.319 --> 00:01:28.179
Everyone with access is listed under People.

21
00:01:28.179 --> 00:01:31.075
If someone leaves, choose Remove.

22
00:01:31.075 --> 00:01:33.531
They lose access right away.

23
00:01:33.984 --> 00:01:37.845
Here’s what joining looks like for a new employee.

24
00:01:37.845 --> 00:01:43.945
After they sign in, they type the code under Join a site, and choose Join site.

25
00:01:44.397 --> 00:01:48.129
Sample Garage now shows up with its published map.

26
00:01:48.129 --> 00:01:52.085
They open it, search for a space, and get directions.

27
00:01:54.593 --> 00:02:01.493
That’s it. Your map is built, published, and your team is on it.
